1
00:00:27,298 --> 00:00:29,200
‎That's right, yesterday…

2
00:00:29,701 --> 00:00:31,002
Hey!

3
00:00:36,674 --> 00:00:40,445
That's right, yesterday… Mariko and I kis…

4
00:00:42,881 --> 00:00:44,115
Kissed…

5
00:01:05,069 --> 00:01:08,339
Huh? What is it?

6
00:01:08,907 --> 00:01:12,544
I'm kind of dizzy, I think…

7
00:01:13,978 --> 00:01:17,048
What? Are you okay?

8
00:01:19,417 --> 00:01:21,186
That was the worst.

9
00:01:34,132 --> 00:01:35,033
Was it a dream?

10
00:01:38,269 --> 00:01:41,105
Part of me wants it to be a dream,
but part of me doesn’t.

11
00:01:53,384 --> 00:01:54,385
Wha-!?

12
00:01:56,354 --> 00:01:59,757
What is it? You're so loud…

13
00:02:06,397 --> 00:02:07,732
I fell asleep, sorry.

14
00:02:07,799 --> 00:02:10,134
You fell asleep? "Sorry"?

15
00:02:11,002 --> 00:02:15,206
I thought I needed to really
hear everything from you.

16
00:02:15,273 --> 00:02:19,143
I didn't know whether to wait for you
to wake up or come back later, and I just…

17
00:02:19,210 --> 00:02:20,645
-I'm sorry.
-Ah, no.

18
00:02:29,220 --> 00:02:32,523
Please tell me everything.

19
00:02:32,590 --> 00:02:34,892
Everything you’ve been doing
without me knowing until now.

20
00:02:34,959 --> 00:02:36,227
In full detail.

21
00:02:39,497 --> 00:02:40,331
‎Okay.

22
00:02:57,615 --> 00:03:02,420
So, the first time I met you

23
00:03:03,254 --> 00:03:04,689
was when I was seven years old.

24
00:03:06,591 --> 00:03:09,060
It was one week
before that kidnapping incident.

25
00:03:11,496 --> 00:03:13,998
On my way home from school, a classmate…

26
00:03:16,067 --> 00:03:19,637
I confessed everything to Mariko.

27
00:03:20,305 --> 00:03:21,606
Every single thing I knew,

28
00:03:21,673 --> 00:03:23,374
-bare and laid out.
-Somebody help!

29
00:03:23,441 --> 00:03:25,743
I felt a self-imposed sense of duty
that I had to protect

30
00:03:27,011 --> 00:03:29,180
you from then on.

31
00:03:29,247 --> 00:03:32,183
Having Mariko listen to the story
of my life could have been

32
00:03:33,217 --> 00:03:37,388
a joyful event, and yet…

33
00:03:39,724 --> 00:03:41,693
because of everything
I’ve done up until now…

34
00:03:44,429 --> 00:03:47,231
it felt like a confession
before receiving a death sentence.

35
00:03:47,298 --> 00:03:50,368
I thought I had to get Tateiwa
to step down from the project,

36
00:03:50,435 --> 00:03:52,804
so I obtained evidence of his misconduct
and went to meet him.

37
00:03:52,870 --> 00:03:53,971
I was like

38
00:03:54,038 --> 00:03:56,074
a criminal climbing the gallows.

39
00:03:56,140 --> 00:03:57,075
Creepy!

40
00:03:57,141 --> 00:03:59,277
-I told you, I won't forgive you.
-Or like

41
00:03:59,344 --> 00:04:03,381
a low-ranking samurai who was ordered
to commit seppuku, but had no subordinate.

42
00:04:04,282 --> 00:04:06,417
Feeling like my stomach was bleeding out,

43
00:04:07,218 --> 00:04:09,520
unable to die.

44
00:04:14,292 --> 00:04:17,628
Even so, talking was
my only way to survive.

45
00:04:19,130 --> 00:04:21,699
So I kept talking.

46
00:04:27,505 --> 00:04:32,577
That's everything.

47
00:04:34,045 --> 00:04:34,879
I'm sorry.

48
00:04:39,884 --> 00:04:40,718
I understand.

49
00:04:42,286 --> 00:04:44,422
I also don’t get it at all.

50
00:04:45,056 --> 00:04:45,923
What?

51
00:04:45,990 --> 00:04:47,358
I’m going to tell you clearly.

52
00:04:48,426 --> 00:04:52,029
First of all, knowing where my home is

53
00:04:52,530 --> 00:04:55,099
and passing in front of it
isn’t something I consider stalking.

54
00:04:55,867 --> 00:04:59,737
When you’re a child, it’s actually quite
common to know where your classmates live

55
00:04:59,804 --> 00:05:04,308
and think, "Ah, that’s her house"
when passing by,

56
00:05:04,375 --> 00:05:06,010
so it isn’t strange at all.

57
00:05:06,911 --> 00:05:08,146
-Thank you.
-However,

58
00:05:09,113 --> 00:05:12,116
coming to the front of my home
specifically to check on

59
00:05:12,183 --> 00:05:14,685
or monitor my actions,

60
00:05:15,453 --> 00:05:18,556
waiting in ambush, or interacting with me
while pretending it's a coincidence,

61
00:05:18,623 --> 00:05:22,260
I feel that kind of behavior
is unacceptable.

62
00:05:24,462 --> 00:05:27,899
-Yes.
-And if you knew I would dislike it,

63
00:05:27,965 --> 00:05:30,868
and you still continued these actions,
that would be, needless to say,

64
00:05:31,502 --> 00:05:33,971
completely unacceptable.
It’s out of the question.

65
00:05:39,610 --> 00:05:40,578
But

66
00:05:41,779 --> 00:05:44,849
I don’t think you would
do something like that.

67
00:05:46,150 --> 00:05:48,653
Because I know you.

68
00:05:50,455 --> 00:05:53,558
In other words, if I had found out
about all these actions

69
00:05:53,624 --> 00:05:55,660
back when I didn’t know you,

70
00:05:56,394 --> 00:05:59,564
I likely would have felt terrified of you.

71
00:06:00,965 --> 00:06:02,867
Even if it was the exact same you.

72
00:06:04,001 --> 00:06:04,869
Yes.

73
00:06:06,070 --> 00:06:06,904
But

74
00:06:07,738 --> 00:06:10,541
now I understand why you were suspected

75
00:06:11,542 --> 00:06:13,878
in Tateiwa and Sayuri's cases.

76
00:06:18,549 --> 00:06:20,952
The incidents are happening all around me.

77
00:06:32,563 --> 00:06:33,731
I’ve decided.

78
00:06:35,233 --> 00:06:37,668
To make sure you don’t do
anything dangerous anymore,

79
00:06:37,735 --> 00:06:40,238
I’m going to stay here
and monitor you for a while.

80
00:06:40,304 --> 00:06:43,741
What? You'll monitor me here?

81
00:06:43,808 --> 00:06:47,345
Besides, Hatano hasn’t been
caught yet, so it’s dangerous, right?

82
00:06:48,212 --> 00:06:51,249
I’m going to live here for a while.

83
00:06:52,383 --> 00:06:53,251
What?

84
00:06:54,619 --> 00:06:55,553
What?

85
00:06:57,889 --> 00:06:58,890
What?

86
00:07:03,528 --> 00:07:06,931
Yesterday, a female office worker
was attacked on her way home,

87
00:07:06,998 --> 00:07:09,433
kidnapped, and held against her will.

88
00:07:10,001 --> 00:07:13,538
The woman was safely
rescued by the police,

89
00:07:13,604 --> 00:07:15,840
but the perpetrator is on the run,

90
00:07:15,907 --> 00:07:18,910
and police continue to search for him.

91
00:07:18,976 --> 00:07:22,013
The suspect on the run
is Satoru Hatano, age 60.

92
00:07:23,114 --> 00:07:25,449
He's still on the run.

93
00:07:26,918 --> 00:07:29,053
What on earth is going on?

94
00:07:30,922 --> 00:07:34,158
Sometimes, Mariko acts in way
I don't understand.

95
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:37,628
Just like that day, in the summer
of seventh grade.

96
00:07:39,297 --> 00:07:40,131
No,

97
00:07:40,631 --> 00:07:43,434
what happened that summer
doesn't matter right now.

98
00:07:43,501 --> 00:07:44,402
Um…

99
00:07:45,937 --> 00:07:47,972
You don't need to force yourself
to watch that.

100
00:07:48,539 --> 00:07:49,840
What are you talking about?

101
00:07:49,907 --> 00:07:52,109
We have to keep track
of the enemy’s moves.

102
00:07:55,279 --> 00:07:56,847
-Ah, hey.
-Yes?

103
00:07:56,914 --> 00:08:00,051
Uh, is it okay if I sleep right here?

104
00:08:00,117 --> 00:08:02,253
Oh, please use the bed.
I’ll sleep on the sofa.

105
00:08:02,320 --> 00:08:04,455
No, it’s fine. It’s your house.

106
00:08:04,522 --> 00:08:05,756
I’ll be okay.

107
00:08:06,757 --> 00:08:07,792
I brought this.

108
00:08:08,459 --> 00:08:10,161
-What's that?
-A sleeping bag.

109
00:08:20,605 --> 00:08:23,240
Mariko is truly incomprehensible.

110
00:08:32,683 --> 00:08:33,718
Hey, stop it.

111
00:08:33,784 --> 00:08:36,754
-What?
-You were staring at me just now, right?

112
00:08:36,821 --> 00:08:38,422
No, no, no, that’s a false accusation.

113
00:08:38,489 --> 00:08:41,659
What? I can’t trust you.
You've been doing this stuff for 25 years.

114
00:08:41,726 --> 00:08:45,096
I will absolutely not cross this line.

115
00:08:45,162 --> 00:08:47,031
I am a man who strictly honors boundaries.

116
00:08:47,098 --> 00:08:48,366
Please rest assured.

117
00:08:54,538 --> 00:08:56,007
What kind of fish do you have?

118
00:08:56,073 --> 00:08:57,375
-What's up?
-Huh?

119
00:08:57,441 --> 00:08:59,010
-What's this? What kind of fish?
-Wait, you're crossing the line.

120
00:08:59,076 --> 00:09:01,145
-I don't have any fish.
-You… You don't?

121
00:09:01,212 --> 00:09:03,047
-They're not very friendly.
-What?

122
00:09:13,791 --> 00:09:14,859
Sota!

123
00:09:16,060 --> 00:09:17,695
I saw on the news
that Hatano is on the run…

124
00:09:17,762 --> 00:09:18,629
Tomoya.

125
00:09:23,834 --> 00:09:24,902
Mariko.

126
00:09:27,738 --> 00:09:29,907
-Thank goodness.
-Tomoya?

127
00:09:31,442 --> 00:09:32,443
Hey.

128
00:09:38,949 --> 00:09:41,118
I'm glad both of you are safe.

129
00:09:42,319 --> 00:09:43,320
Really.

130
00:09:44,955 --> 00:09:45,790
Tomoya?

131
00:09:47,825 --> 00:09:49,293
Ah, sorry, sorry.

132
00:09:51,529 --> 00:09:54,298
Wait, so, does this mean you two are…

133
00:09:55,199 --> 00:09:56,701
-Ah, no, uh…
-Uh…

134
00:09:56,767 --> 00:09:59,170
-It's dangerous, so--
-Ah, got it, got it. I'll leave then.

135
00:09:59,236 --> 00:10:00,771
-Wait, wait…
-See you!

136
00:10:01,338 --> 00:10:03,107
I'm leaving. Don't worry.

137
00:10:19,323 --> 00:10:22,426
-What?
-Quiet!

138
00:10:22,493 --> 00:10:26,897
Yukimura saved you 25 years ago?

139
00:10:28,065 --> 00:10:28,966
Yes.

140
00:10:29,667 --> 00:10:32,470
That must be destiny.

141
00:10:32,536 --> 00:10:33,904
You said there's no such thing as destiny.

142
00:10:33,971 --> 00:10:36,474
-I take it back. There is.
-That was quick.

143
00:10:38,175 --> 00:10:42,146
Still, I feel like it's
pretty different from destiny.

144
00:10:43,614 --> 00:10:46,484
I mean, I haven't actually said
I forgive him or anything.

145
00:10:47,651 --> 00:10:49,987
I shouldn't let my guard down yet.

146
00:10:51,922 --> 00:10:54,992
I don't really get what you mean,
but anyway, Mariko,

147
00:10:55,726 --> 00:10:57,394
you should stop seeing two men at once.

148
00:10:57,461 --> 00:10:58,662
That's bad manners.

149
00:11:00,064 --> 00:11:01,065
What are you talking about?

150
00:11:01,132 --> 00:11:02,933
Your phone's ringing, isn't it?

151
00:11:03,501 --> 00:11:05,903
TAISUKE SAKURA

152
00:11:05,970 --> 00:11:07,872
TAISUKE SAKURA: 13 MISSED CALLS

153
00:11:17,515 --> 00:11:18,349
Whoa…

154
00:11:18,883 --> 00:11:21,485
WHERE ARE YOU?
I SHOULD BE WITH YOU FOR SAFETY.

155
00:11:22,052 --> 00:11:24,588
TAISUKE SAKURA

156
00:11:26,023 --> 00:11:27,691
Excuse me for a second.

157
00:11:40,004 --> 00:11:40,938
Yes, hello?

158
00:11:42,339 --> 00:11:44,742
No, I'm sorry,

159
00:11:44,809 --> 00:11:47,044
I didn’t notice you were calling.

160
00:11:47,111 --> 00:11:49,480
Where did you go yesterday?

161
00:11:50,181 --> 00:11:52,116
It must be scary to be alone, isn't it?

162
00:11:53,350 --> 00:11:56,821
We don't know
when Hatano will attack again.

163
00:12:04,895 --> 00:12:07,298
I'm on Team Yukimura.

164
00:12:07,932 --> 00:12:09,166
Me too.

165
00:12:10,701 --> 00:12:13,671
I mean, what's going on with you two?

166
00:12:15,472 --> 00:12:19,343
I’m probably right on the edge
of a boundary right now.

167
00:12:20,044 --> 00:12:21,745
-A boundary.
-The edge.

168
00:12:21,812 --> 00:12:25,616
You say that,
but the enemy is pressing in hard.

169
00:12:26,550 --> 00:12:29,019
Isn’t that the detective?

170
00:12:29,086 --> 00:12:30,921
Seriously, isn’t he amazing?

171
00:12:30,988 --> 00:12:33,390
I would have given up long ago.

172
00:12:33,958 --> 00:12:36,093
Your enemy is incredibly persistent.

173
00:12:36,727 --> 00:12:38,462
You can't just leave him unchecked.

174
00:12:39,964 --> 00:12:41,832
-No.
-See you.

175
00:12:47,938 --> 00:12:50,007
Yes. Goodbye.

176
00:13:01,051 --> 00:13:02,353
FATHER

177
00:13:06,857 --> 00:13:07,892
Hello?

178
00:13:11,428 --> 00:13:12,496
I'm coming too!

179
00:13:14,899 --> 00:13:18,936
Because I snitched on Yukimura
just to save myself,

180
00:13:19,837 --> 00:13:22,072
I put both of you in danger.

181
00:13:23,107 --> 00:13:26,343
I am truly sorry.

182
00:13:26,410 --> 00:13:28,345
It’s not your fault, Asai.

183
00:13:29,113 --> 00:13:29,947
Right.

184
00:13:31,248 --> 00:13:32,883
It's all my fault.

185
00:13:37,021 --> 00:13:37,955
Asai.

186
00:13:40,557 --> 00:13:41,392
I'm sorry.

187
00:13:43,527 --> 00:13:45,462
Both the kidnapping 25 years ago

188
00:13:46,597 --> 00:13:47,965
and now this.

189
00:13:50,534 --> 00:13:52,202
It's all my fault.

190
00:13:54,505 --> 00:13:55,439
What do you mean?

191
00:13:58,442 --> 00:14:00,177
You were targeted

192
00:14:02,680 --> 00:14:04,481
because you are my daughter.

193
00:14:06,951 --> 00:14:11,622
Hatano and I
were classmates in elementary school.

194
00:14:13,557 --> 00:14:14,458
What?

195
00:14:14,959 --> 00:14:17,227
Right before that kidnapping incident,

196
00:14:18,762 --> 00:14:21,065
there was an elementary school reunion.

197
00:14:21,699 --> 00:14:22,967
And it was there

198
00:14:24,535 --> 00:14:26,303
-that I reunited with Hatano.
-See you!

199
00:14:29,440 --> 00:14:30,441
Gin and tonic.

200
00:14:32,343 --> 00:14:33,777
Hey, Nose.

201
00:14:34,345 --> 00:14:39,183
You couldn't exactly say
Hatano's family was well off.

202
00:14:40,851 --> 00:14:43,287
He always wore the same clothes,

203
00:14:44,521 --> 00:14:46,123
and he was made fun of.

204
00:14:49,760 --> 00:14:51,662
I heard you’ll be
the company president soon?

205
00:14:53,630 --> 00:14:54,498
Yes.

206
00:14:55,299 --> 00:14:58,535
Things are tough at my dad’s factory.

207
00:14:58,602 --> 00:15:03,340
I instantly assumed
he was trying to beg for money.

208
00:15:03,407 --> 00:15:08,412
Sorry, but just because we were classmates
doesn’t mean you can rely on me.

209
00:15:09,213 --> 00:15:13,083
I know things have been rough for you
because of your father, though.

210
00:15:16,720 --> 00:15:18,555
People really don’t change, do they?

211
00:15:20,257 --> 00:15:25,129
I was more pissed off at you than the guys
who actually bullied me back then.

212
00:15:26,430 --> 00:15:28,165
You said to the guys who were bullying me,

213
00:15:28,832 --> 00:15:32,302
"Don't discriminate against someone
because of their family.

214
00:15:32,369 --> 00:15:37,241
Life is determined
by what kind of parents you’re born to."

215
00:15:37,908 --> 00:15:38,909
Right?

216
00:15:39,643 --> 00:15:41,345
Terrible, right?

217
00:15:43,147 --> 00:15:44,848
What’s even more terrible…

218
00:15:48,185 --> 00:15:50,888
is that I didn’t even remember saying it.

219
00:15:54,124 --> 00:15:57,661
"If life changes based on what
kind of parents you are born to…"

220
00:15:59,596 --> 00:16:03,267
Then your daughter
will face the consequences

221
00:16:03,867 --> 00:16:05,636
of being born to you.

222
00:16:09,773 --> 00:16:12,709
Hatano committed his first kidnapping

223
00:16:13,277 --> 00:16:15,546
three days after that reunion.

224
00:16:17,548 --> 00:16:21,885
It is my fault
that everyone was dragged into this.

225
00:16:23,454 --> 00:16:25,422
And yet I tried to hide it.

226
00:16:28,559 --> 00:16:30,327
I am so sorry.

227
00:16:43,107 --> 00:16:47,010
He asked a friend in the police

228
00:16:47,077 --> 00:16:50,647
not to make public the fact
that he had a personal connection

229
00:16:50,714 --> 00:16:51,548
with Hatano.

230
00:16:55,953 --> 00:16:56,820
Thanks.

231
00:16:57,554 --> 00:17:00,224
Both of them were apologetic, Yukimura.

232
00:17:01,024 --> 00:17:04,261
They said they want to apologize to you
in person next time.

233
00:17:06,530 --> 00:17:09,233
Hatano might not even know
what he’s doing anymore.

234
00:17:10,300 --> 00:17:11,502
What?

235
00:17:11,568 --> 00:17:14,872
People can’t live without something
to support them, right?

236
00:17:16,440 --> 00:17:21,345
If Hatano is supporting himself through
resentment or obsession toward someone,

237
00:17:21,411 --> 00:17:23,647
maybe the target could be anyone.

238
00:17:24,715 --> 00:17:27,751
So, why couldn't it just be me?

239
00:17:29,386 --> 00:17:32,189
He might still resent the president,

240
00:17:33,323 --> 00:17:37,060
or maybe he’s just forcibly
clinging to the emotion

241
00:17:37,127 --> 00:17:38,929
of resentment at this point.

242
00:17:41,665 --> 00:17:45,435
-Ah, it’s fine. I’ll do it.
-Oh, thank you.

243
00:17:45,502 --> 00:17:46,336
Here.

244
00:18:08,492 --> 00:18:10,093
Man, I'm hungry now.

245
00:18:10,861 --> 00:18:13,664
-Mariko, do you usually cook at home--
-Hey!

246
00:18:14,198 --> 00:18:16,333
-Stop doing that!
-Doing what?

247
00:18:16,400 --> 00:18:19,336
Every time I put a condiment back,
you turn the label forward like this.

248
00:18:19,403 --> 00:18:22,539
-You’re sneakily straightening them up!
-That's just a habit…

249
00:18:22,606 --> 00:18:24,808
If you want them facing forward,
you could just tell me.

250
00:18:24,875 --> 00:18:26,243
Fixing them behind my back…

251
00:18:26,843 --> 00:18:27,878
-That's just sly.
-No,

252
00:18:27,945 --> 00:18:32,149
-I didn't mean it like that.
-Ah, right! Of course.

253
00:18:32,216 --> 00:18:34,718
You love doing things
behind people's backs, don't you?

254
00:18:34,785 --> 00:18:36,753
-That's right.
-No, no.

255
00:18:36,820 --> 00:18:38,522
Let me ask you this.

256
00:18:38,589 --> 00:18:41,692
Even though you know I was fixing them,

257
00:18:41,758 --> 00:18:43,427
-you still put them down the wrong way?
-Yes.

258
00:18:43,493 --> 00:18:44,761
"Yes"?

259
00:18:46,129 --> 00:18:48,031
What's wrong with that?

260
00:18:48,599 --> 00:18:53,270
Ah, besides, I was planning
to align them all at the end.

261
00:18:53,337 --> 00:18:54,538
You just said "Ah'!"

262
00:18:54,605 --> 00:18:57,441
That's because
you only thought of that just now.

263
00:18:57,507 --> 00:18:59,309
You're being annoying!

264
00:19:01,044 --> 00:19:02,045
Annoying?

265
00:19:03,347 --> 00:19:04,348
You're one to talk.

266
00:19:23,767 --> 00:19:25,369
TAISUKE SAKURA

267
00:19:37,948 --> 00:19:41,018
I’ve been invited
to go to an art exhibition.

268
00:19:41,885 --> 00:19:43,820
-An art exhibition?
-Yes.

269
00:19:44,988 --> 00:19:45,856
To see paintings.

270
00:19:47,758 --> 00:19:50,227
-What do you think?
-What do I think?

271
00:19:51,895 --> 00:19:53,997
Mariko, you aren't even
interested in paintings, right?

272
00:19:54,765 --> 00:19:57,601
What? Why? I am interested.

273
00:19:58,168 --> 00:19:59,636
You're a total liar.

274
00:20:00,137 --> 00:20:02,639
A long time ago, when you went
to an art exhibition with your mother…

275
00:20:09,546 --> 00:20:11,381
Mariko, you don't want to see?

276
00:20:11,448 --> 00:20:12,783
No, it's okay.

277
00:20:13,583 --> 00:20:16,019
You got bored really quickly
and started reading a book, right?

278
00:20:19,122 --> 00:20:20,457
You were watching that too?

279
00:20:24,061 --> 00:20:24,928
Sorry.

280
00:20:28,065 --> 00:20:30,600
My mother loved paintings.

281
00:20:33,503 --> 00:20:35,872
Because my mother loved them,
I wanted to love them too.

282
00:20:39,343 --> 00:20:41,912
Spending time thinking about
the things my mother loved

283
00:20:43,146 --> 00:20:45,515
feels like spending time with her.

284
00:20:51,788 --> 00:20:54,891
I sounded a bit
like you just now, Yukimura.

285
00:21:08,705 --> 00:21:09,873
Is it good?

286
00:21:09,940 --> 00:21:12,175
Oh, sorry, it's very good.

287
00:21:12,909 --> 00:21:13,877
I forgot to say it.

288
00:21:13,944 --> 00:21:15,045
You were just quietly eating.

289
00:21:15,112 --> 00:21:16,046
Sorry.

290
00:21:43,039 --> 00:21:45,208
Yukimura, how much do you know?

291
00:21:47,210 --> 00:21:48,245
What?

292
00:21:49,880 --> 00:21:53,550
My mother was suspected
of having an affair.

293
00:21:55,452 --> 00:21:57,454
I didn't believe it, of course.

294
00:21:59,356 --> 00:22:00,524
There's no way.

295
00:22:02,426 --> 00:22:04,127
My mother wasn't that type of person.

296
00:22:07,998 --> 00:22:09,132
But…

297
00:22:10,467 --> 00:22:13,837
I wonder whose exhibition that was.

298
00:22:15,005 --> 00:22:16,840
Who was she going to meet there?

299
00:22:20,243 --> 00:22:22,979
Maybe there was a side to my mother
that I didn’t know about.

300
00:22:26,650 --> 00:22:30,387
I hated that thought for a long time
and was scared of it,

301
00:22:33,390 --> 00:22:36,026
but now that I’ve reached this age,

302
00:22:37,027 --> 00:22:39,629
I’ve made peace with the fact
that people have different sides.

303
00:22:42,365 --> 00:22:44,201
I think the facet your mother showed you

304
00:22:45,335 --> 00:22:48,638
was also part of her true self.

305
00:22:54,444 --> 00:22:55,579
Yes.

306
00:22:59,015 --> 00:23:00,283
Thank you.

307
00:23:24,908 --> 00:23:26,343
MARIKO WENT TO LOOK
AT PAINTINGS WITH HER MOTHER

308
00:23:52,002 --> 00:23:55,972
-What are you doing?
-No, nothing.

309
00:23:59,543 --> 00:24:03,246
HATANO

310
00:24:03,313 --> 00:24:06,249
I'VE BEEN THINKING ABOUT
HATANO A LOT LATELY

311
00:24:34,044 --> 00:24:36,913
WHY IS THE CAFE CLOSED?

312
00:24:36,980 --> 00:24:40,183
DID SOMETHING HAPPEN?

313
00:25:08,244 --> 00:25:10,447
Hey, kid.

314
00:25:37,140 --> 00:25:40,010
Why don't we settle this already?

315
00:26:08,038 --> 00:26:08,938
Tomoya.

316
00:26:22,419 --> 00:26:23,253
Tomoya.

317
00:26:24,921 --> 00:26:27,257
Stop it. Tomoya, Tomoya.

318
00:26:27,323 --> 00:26:28,892
Stop, Tomoya!

319
00:26:34,497 --> 00:26:36,332
Do you know someone named Mizuki Sagara?

320
00:26:36,900 --> 00:26:37,734
Huh?

321
00:26:38,535 --> 00:26:40,203
Who's that?

322
00:26:45,775 --> 00:26:46,976
You don't remember?

323
00:26:48,344 --> 00:26:50,180
The poor girl whose life ended…

324
00:26:53,216 --> 00:26:54,884
at just nine years old because of you.

325
00:26:56,086 --> 00:26:58,054
You don't remember her?

326
00:27:03,593 --> 00:27:05,829
Tomoya, that's enough. Tomoya.

327
00:27:05,895 --> 00:27:07,097
Tomoya, stop!

328
00:27:07,163 --> 00:27:08,231
-What are you doing?
-Shut up! Get off me!

329
00:27:08,298 --> 00:27:10,400
-Tomoya!
-Die.

330
00:27:10,467 --> 00:27:12,335
-Tomoya!
-Die!

331
00:27:12,402 --> 00:27:13,369
-Hey!
-What are you doing?

332
00:27:14,671 --> 00:27:16,039
Let go of him. Let go!

333
00:27:16,106 --> 00:27:17,006
Hey!

334
00:27:17,941 --> 00:27:19,476
-Don't mess with me!
-Stop!

335
00:27:20,877 --> 00:27:22,545
Don't mess with me!

336
00:27:23,947 --> 00:27:24,948
-Stop.
-Hey!

337
00:27:27,150 --> 00:27:27,984
Stop!

338
00:27:47,270 --> 00:27:50,607
Why am I the only one being arrested?

339
00:27:51,274 --> 00:27:53,543
Man, the world is unfair!

340
00:27:53,610 --> 00:27:56,045
-Shut up already.
-What's wrong with you?

341
00:27:56,980 --> 00:27:57,814
Come on.

342
00:27:58,815 --> 00:28:02,786
Listen, rich people are unfair!

343
00:28:03,887 --> 00:28:05,822
You’re all eyesores.

344
00:28:05,889 --> 00:28:06,856
What's with all of you?

345
00:28:06,923 --> 00:28:08,892
-Hey.
-Calm down, calm down.

346
00:28:08,958 --> 00:28:10,026
What?

347
00:28:13,830 --> 00:28:15,465
You're the eyesore here.

348
00:28:18,735 --> 00:28:20,236
If it weren't for you…

349
00:28:23,773 --> 00:28:25,041
-Sakura!
-That's enough.

350
00:28:25,608 --> 00:28:26,476
Stop it.

351
00:28:44,761 --> 00:28:45,895
Thank you very much.

352
00:28:53,336 --> 00:28:56,806
For now, they said I won't be prosecuted,
but they chewed me out for going too far.

353
00:28:59,242 --> 00:29:00,944
Don't look at me like that.

354
00:29:03,980 --> 00:29:05,715
Hey, there’s a place I want to go.

355
00:29:06,516 --> 00:29:07,617
Mind coming with me?

356
00:29:23,533 --> 00:29:24,767
Coffee's ready.

357
00:29:56,165 --> 00:29:59,469
Ah, here. I know it's important to you.

358
00:30:09,078 --> 00:30:09,979
Tomoya.

359
00:30:12,649 --> 00:30:15,518
How much did you know, and for how long?

360
00:30:20,823 --> 00:30:24,727
At first, it was Mariko.

361
00:30:27,330 --> 00:30:30,133
There were guys spreading rumors
that the daughter of the president

362
00:30:30,199 --> 00:30:31,668
of Nose Cosmetics was one year above us.

363
00:30:32,869 --> 00:30:36,706
Right away, it clicked that she was
the girl from my sister's incident.

364
00:30:40,310 --> 00:30:42,645
"Ah, I was so glad she was alive."

365
00:30:44,948 --> 00:30:47,517
"You survived, and have grown up."

366
00:30:48,217 --> 00:30:49,652
That's what I thought.

367
00:30:49,719 --> 00:30:52,388
Tomoya. Over here!

368
00:31:00,163 --> 00:31:03,066
After that, every time
I saw Mariko on campus,

369
00:31:03,132 --> 00:31:04,334
I couldn’t help but notice her.

370
00:31:06,970 --> 00:31:08,171
But

371
00:31:09,372 --> 00:31:11,741
there was always one guy
who entered my field of vision.

372
00:31:18,748 --> 00:31:20,583
You two didn't seem to be acquaintances.

373
00:31:24,687 --> 00:31:25,855
So I got kind of curious.

374
00:31:32,295 --> 00:31:34,163
-You like that girl, don't you?
-What?

375
00:31:35,231 --> 00:31:36,466
I can tell by looking at you.

376
00:31:37,300 --> 00:31:38,568
No, no, no, that's not…

377
00:31:39,602 --> 00:31:40,837
-You're so easy to read!
-What?

378
00:31:47,944 --> 00:31:48,978
Why?

379
00:31:56,152 --> 00:31:59,522
Why did you have to live your life
carrying so much pain, Tomoya?

380
00:32:02,825 --> 00:32:04,494
You're always cheerful,

381
00:32:06,095 --> 00:32:09,165
kind, thoughtful.

382
00:32:11,300 --> 00:32:13,703
Compared to me,
you're a far better human being.

383
00:32:15,772 --> 00:32:17,240
You're an amazing guy!

384
00:32:18,608 --> 00:32:20,777
You’re such a good guy, Tomoya!

385
00:32:20,843 --> 00:32:22,545
So why did you have to be hurt like this?

386
00:32:26,315 --> 00:32:27,316
Come on.

387
00:32:29,452 --> 00:32:30,420
You’ve…

388
00:32:33,723 --> 00:32:35,758
supported me all this time.

389
00:32:40,396 --> 00:32:42,365
Even though

390
00:32:42,432 --> 00:32:45,902
you found out things that should
have made you abandon me long ago,

391
00:32:47,437 --> 00:32:49,038
you still stayed by my side.

392
00:32:54,277 --> 00:32:57,880
So why have you been
suffering this whole time, Tomoya?

393
00:33:00,283 --> 00:33:01,417
Why?

394
00:33:05,721 --> 00:33:07,757
Why did you have to be
the one to get hurt?

395
00:33:13,296 --> 00:33:14,764
I couldn’t do anything.

396
00:33:18,468 --> 00:33:19,502
You were always by my side…

397
00:33:24,440 --> 00:33:26,309
listening to me, and yet…

398
00:33:27,276 --> 00:33:30,646
And yet I didn't notice a thing.
What was I doing?

399
00:33:31,414 --> 00:33:33,349
I can't forgive myself. I really can't.

400
00:33:36,285 --> 00:33:37,353
I'm sorry, Tomoya.

401
00:33:39,822 --> 00:33:40,823
‎I'm sorry.

402
00:33:44,794 --> 00:33:46,095
‎What's that for?

403
00:33:47,864 --> 00:33:49,198
Why are you apologizing?

404
00:33:58,441 --> 00:34:00,510
It's not like I've lived
with hatred nonstop.

405
00:34:01,911 --> 00:34:04,447
There were times I forgot
about the incident and Hatano.

406
00:34:07,116 --> 00:34:08,284
Or rather…

407
00:34:10,520 --> 00:34:13,089
I learned to live without
constantly remembering it.

408
00:34:17,059 --> 00:34:18,027
But…

409
00:34:19,328 --> 00:34:21,931
when I found out Mariko
and you were attacked…

410
00:34:27,570 --> 00:34:30,606
a rage I’d never felt
before rushed over me.

411
00:34:32,942 --> 00:34:36,279
I figured I'd rather kill him than let
those precious to me be killed again.

412
00:34:43,753 --> 00:34:45,087
Pretty crazy, right?

413
00:34:46,989 --> 00:34:49,058
To think I had such
crazy emotions inside me.

414
00:35:01,537 --> 00:35:03,706
I’m not a decent human being at all.

415
00:35:06,542 --> 00:35:10,346
I was just grinning the whole time
so nobody would notice.

416
00:35:10,413 --> 00:35:12,582
No. That's not true.

417
00:35:14,650 --> 00:35:17,019
I'm sorry, Tomoya.
I couldn't do anything for you.

418
00:35:30,566 --> 00:35:33,636
It's probably because you're like this
that we've been together all this time.

419
00:35:37,306 --> 00:35:39,575
Well, I guess I'm pretty much
the only one who could stay with you.

420
00:35:52,188 --> 00:35:53,923
-Hey!
-What are you doing?

421
00:35:53,990 --> 00:35:55,391
-I'm trying to go home.
-Let's go together.

422
00:35:55,458 --> 00:35:56,359
No, no, no.

423
00:35:57,260 --> 00:35:58,794
Why do you want to go home alone?

424
00:35:58,861 --> 00:35:59,695
I texted you.

425
00:35:59,762 --> 00:36:00,963
-You didn't.
-I did.

426
00:36:35,231 --> 00:36:37,033
Tomoya!

427
00:36:45,875 --> 00:36:49,178
Come on. What were you doing?

428
00:36:50,179 --> 00:36:51,147
Idiot.

429
00:36:54,650 --> 00:36:55,885
Sorry.

430
00:36:59,021 --> 00:36:59,989
I'm sorry.

431
00:37:04,960 --> 00:37:06,362
I'm home…

432
00:37:20,142 --> 00:37:23,012
I'M AT MY FAMILY'S HOUSE
I'LL BE HOME LATE

433
00:37:40,262 --> 00:37:44,100
I wonder whose exhibition that was.

434
00:37:45,167 --> 00:37:47,136
Who was she going to meet there?

435
00:37:59,382 --> 00:38:01,417
-Mariko, you don't want to see?
-July 12th.

436
00:38:01,484 --> 00:38:03,119
‎No, it's okay.

437
00:38:03,185 --> 00:38:06,789
Mariko went to look
at paintings with her mother.

438
00:38:09,458 --> 00:38:14,697
Mariko's mother
was talking happily with a painter,

439
00:38:14,764 --> 00:38:17,166
but Mariko didn’t seem interested.

440
00:38:35,484 --> 00:38:40,656
Today, I saw Mariko's mother
get angry at the florist.

441
00:38:42,925 --> 00:38:45,995
He apologized over and over
for breaking the vase.

442
00:38:46,562 --> 00:38:50,399
She scolded the florist
for not worrying about his own injury.

443
00:38:50,466 --> 00:38:53,169
It made me think she's similar to Mariko.

444
00:38:59,208 --> 00:39:01,310
WORRYING ABOUT HIS OWN INJURY

445
00:39:27,703 --> 00:39:28,704
Mariko.

446
00:39:30,306 --> 00:39:32,641
There's something else
I need to talk with you about.

447
00:39:42,218 --> 00:39:43,686
It's about the secret

448
00:39:44,753 --> 00:39:47,289
between me and Sayuri,
which you asked about.

449
00:40:00,069 --> 00:40:04,006
I’m sorry to bother you at work,
but there's something I'd like to ask.

450
00:40:04,740 --> 00:40:06,108
Wait, you were here the other day?

451
00:40:06,175 --> 00:40:07,977
-Hello!
-Yes.

452
00:40:08,611 --> 00:40:09,545
Twenty-five years ago,

453
00:40:09,612 --> 00:40:12,414
was there someone named
Taisuke Sakura working here?

454
00:40:13,415 --> 00:40:14,617
There was.

455
00:40:15,784 --> 00:40:17,253
Why is everyone asking about that?

456
00:40:17,887 --> 00:40:19,355
I wonder whose exhibition that was.

457
00:40:19,421 --> 00:40:21,123
She was talking happily with a painter.

458
00:40:21,190 --> 00:40:23,125
I saw her get angry at the florist.

459
00:40:23,192 --> 00:40:26,095
She scolded the florist for not worrying
about his own injury.

460
00:40:26,161 --> 00:40:29,698
Is the world really full of coincidences?

461
00:40:29,765 --> 00:40:33,102
I have to protect her from you.

462
00:40:34,003 --> 00:40:39,275
If only you hadn't loved her,
you wouldn't have ended up a criminal.

463
00:40:43,178 --> 00:40:44,246
Thank you very much.

464
00:41:10,973 --> 00:41:13,242
‎KYOKO NOSE

465
00:41:24,920 --> 00:41:25,955
Yes, hello?

466
00:41:28,390 --> 00:41:31,193
Yes. I understand.

467
00:41:33,195 --> 00:41:37,099
I would like to speak with you too.

468
00:41:40,035 --> 00:41:41,170
I'll be waiting.

469
00:41:58,087 --> 00:42:00,022
Stop it already!

470
00:42:05,394 --> 00:42:06,962
I'm at my limit.

471
00:42:11,066 --> 00:42:11,934
You…

472
00:42:14,970 --> 00:42:16,205
It was you.

473
00:42:18,073 --> 00:42:19,708
You kidnapped Mariko.

474
00:42:25,080 --> 00:42:26,315
Why…

475
00:42:28,350 --> 00:42:30,953
Why? Why? Why!?

476
00:42:33,389 --> 00:42:35,124
Why would you say something like that?

477
00:42:43,465 --> 00:42:44,533
Forgive me.

478
00:44:15,324 --> 00:44:18,961
And so, the door containing
all the secrets was opened.

479
00:44:21,230 --> 00:44:22,598
But I could no longer…

480
00:44:24,800 --> 00:44:27,236
protect Mariko.

481
00:44:29,037 --> 00:44:30,439
Don't mess with me!

482
00:44:31,073 --> 00:44:33,475
‎NEXT TIME…

483
00:44:38,046 --> 00:44:38,981
‎Subtitle translation by: Maslin Friedman

